格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Web UI polish layer for DeepSeek Harness: normalizes unfinished or self-contradictory official UI, reconciles style conflicts between installed plugins, and unifies the visual language via official design tokens.","id":"gh:1335011656","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-ui-harmonizer","slug":"Physicolor/dsh-ui-harmonizer","topics":["browser-extension","cordis","cordis-plugin","deepseek-harness","design-resources","design-system","dsh","dsh-plugin","plugin","plugins","ui-enhancement","ui-harmonizer","web-ui"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Web UI polish layer for DeepSeek Harness: normalizes unfinished or self-contradictory official UI, r"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"econciles style conflicts between installed plugins, and unifies the visual language via official de"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"yle conflicts between installed plugins, and unifies the visual language via official design tokens."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"description: \"One interface language for the Harness, plus per-plugin reconciliation and a read-only"},{"id":"p2s2","text":" compatibility audit.\""},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English · 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"DSH UI Harmonizer"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"UI harmonizer for DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Normalizes the official UI · reconciles every plugin · settings auto-normalizer · UI customization ("},{"id":"p6s2","text":"width, fonts, panel glide)"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Part of DSH Design System — this repository is the runtime half."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"The spec it enforces lives at Physicolor/dsh-design-resources."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"> **TL;DR:** You installed a bunch of DSH plugins but the UI looks inconsistent? DSH UI Harmonizer u"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ses **CSS overrides + runtime DOM coordination** to bring them back to the official design language "},{"id":"p9s3","text":"— **non-destructive, fully reversible, zero model cost**."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"DSH UI Harmonizer is a **client-only DSH bundle plugin**. It adds no model tools and modifies no ses"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"sion logs — it adjusts the UI purely through official slots (`settings.section` / `settings.general."},{"id":"p10s3","text":"item`) and the `--dsw-*` semantic token system."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### 🎨 Official UI Normalization"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| Capability | Detail |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Single-line header | Moves the conversation / trajectory selector into the title row; the header c"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"ollapses to one line |\n| Button capsule family | Session log, widgets, and toggle buttons unified in"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"to 32px capsules |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"The plugin is organised by **target**, not by file type. It exists to harmonize two\ndifferent things"},{"id":"p16s2","text":" at once — (a) the DSH shell itself and (b) whichever community\nplugins happen to be installed next "},{"id":"p16s3","text":"to it — so every source file belongs to exactly\none of four layers:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Layer | Answers | Examples |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| `core/` | infrastructure true regardless of DSH or any plugin | state model + persistence, the Har"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"mony Contract, i18n, DOM/React helpers |\n| `harness/` | normalizations and repairs aimed at the **DS"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"H shell** | official control-recipe mirrors, the settings-header reconciler, the chat-width channel,"},{"id":"p18s4","text":" the frame's column-track transition, menu width, the stylesheet keeper, native-title tooltips, the "},{"id":"p18s5","text":"rounded center card |\n| `plugins/<package>/` | adaptations written for **one** community plugin | `c"},{"id":"p18s6","text":"ommandcode-provider` text normalisation, `dsh-widgets` rail squeeze + handle re-anchor, `dsh-better-"},{"id":"p18s7","text":"sidebar` panels, `dsh-genui` width hygiene |\n| `self/` | the plugin's **own** UI | Settings → Genera"},{"id":"p18s8","text":"l rows, the font selector, the Harmony Doctor page |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Stylesheets follow the same split: 29 `.module.css` fragments with a single entry\n(`src/client/style"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"s/index.ts`) whose **import order is the cascade order**."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The rest of the contract is unchanged:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- **Zero model cost**: the host (node) half is a no-op; all changes happen in the browser half;\n- **"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"Official design tokens**: all styles use the `--dsw-*` semantic tokens and follow light/dark themes "},{"id":"p21s3","text":"automatically;\n- **Two injection channels**: static rules (CSS Modules) + dynamic `<style data-plugi"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"n>` tags;\n- **Reversible cleanup**: every `ctx.effect` returns a disposer, so stopping the plugin le"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"aves no residue — including DOM nodes it relocated and third-party strings it rewrote;\n- **Slot inte"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"gration**: `settings.general.item` / `settings.section` / `shell.overlay`."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Guards live in `scripts/`: `tools/css-baseline.mjs` (byte-invariant of the compiled\nstylesheet), `ve"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"rify-frame-track.cjs` (column-track animation + panel glide),\n`verify-rapid-toggle.cjs` (the glide's"},{"id":"p22s3","text":" re-entrancy: overlapping toggles must leave\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- DeepSeek Harness `0.1.0-rc.6` and compatible later `0.1.x`;\n- Integrates via official slots, coexi"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"sting with better-sidebar, dsh-widgets, dshmarket, etc. by slot order;\n- Known reconciliation target"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"s: `dsh-better-sidebar`, `dsh-widgets`, `dsh-context`, `dsh-notification`, `dshmarket`;\n- The page f"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"ully restores to defaults after uninstall/disable — no residue."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### v0.9.0 — repositioned: from CSS patch to UI contract layer + compatibility auditor"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"**New — Harmony Contract (cross-plugin UI contract)**"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- 🧭 Publishes negotiation variables on `<html>` that any plugin or theme can read without depending "},{"id":"p27s2","text":"on this one: `--enhc-contract` (revision), `--enhc-surface-solid`, `--enhc-glass-aware`, `--enhc-sol"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"id-fill`, `--enhc-content-width`, `--enhc-sidebar-scale`.\n- 🔌 Provides `ctx.get('uiHarmony')` using "},{"id":"p27s4","text":"the product's own `ctx.reflect.provide` idiom (the same one behind `ctx.sidebarRight`): neighbours *"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"*declare** what they occupy with `registerSurface({ id, role, occupies, widthVariable, transition, t"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"okens, opaque })` instead of being measured by guesswork. This plugin only arbitrates and reports; i"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"t declares its own surface too (the Settings → General rows and the UI Compatibility page).\n- 🪟 **Ma"},{"id":"p27s8","text":"terial awareness** derived from the semantic tokens themselves (alpha of `--dsw-alias-bg-base` / `-l"},{"id":"p27s9","text":"ayer-1` / `--dsw-specific-sidebar-fill`), never from plugin identity. Under a glass theme `--enhc-so"},{"id":"p27s10","text":"lid-fill` becomes `transparent`, so the header/panels stop painting an unblurred opaque rectangle ov"},{"id":"p27s11","text":"er the glass. **Measured by simulation** (no third-party theme installed): overriding `--dsw-alias-b"},{"id":"p27s12","text":"g-base` to `rgba(255,255,255,0.45)` flips `--enhc-glass-aware` 0 to 1, `--enhc-surface-solid` 1 to 0"},{"id":"p27s13","text":", `--enhc-solid-fill` to `transparent`, and the session header `background-color` from `rgb(255,255,"},{"id":"p27s14","text":"255)` to `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)`; removing the override restores all four."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"**New — Harmony Doctor (local read-only compatibility audit)**"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- 🩺 Settings → **UI Compatibility**: one click runs four checks, zero network, zero model calls, exp"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"orts a Markdown report.\n- 🕳️ **Dead-rule ledger**: every one of the plugin's own selectors is match-"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"counted, and a selector counts as dead only when it matched nothing in **every view observed** — the"},{"id":"p29s4","text":" ledger persists per view, so the verdict sharpens as the user moves around. Measured over six probe"},{"id":"p29s5","text":" views (hero, settings, session, doctor, glass on, glass off): of 149 selectors, **64 match in at le"},{"id":"p29s6","text":"ast one view and 85 match in none of the observed views**.\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

